&lt;p&gt;This individual will own the long-view strategic planning across the game’s Features ensuring alignment between strategic vision and tactical execution. Key responsibilities include:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the business performance of the Features function, accountable for delivering game KPIs and guiding decisions which drive sustainable long term growth.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own every aspect of a roadmap that achieves KPI goals set by you and the Product Team. Guiding cross-functional partners such as game designers, UX designers and artists to deliver a product that meets the product’s vision and strategy&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Formulate product strategy and create engaging game mechanics and core game loops&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;See feature development through from concept to launch, including post launch analysis and optimization, to deliver best in class features that achieve set KPI goals&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead engagement and monetisation for major feature releases, coordinating across disciplines to ensure smooth, high-impact launches which hit KPI targets.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Monitor the health of the product ecosystem, using insights to proactively identify opportunities and risks, and implement impactful features and initiatives&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify and create process improvements to support feature development&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build a high-performing team, mentoring product managers and operational staff, scaling team capabilities, and fostering a culture of ownership and excellence.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Establish institutional knowledge through clear documentation of experiments, retrospectives, and playbooks to ensure consistent learning and improvement.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Conduct quantitative analyses of data to provide key insights into product performance and uncover opportunities for further engagement and monetization&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Leverage player feedback and game data to inform roadmap and feature design solutions. Use competitive market research to identify future opportunities and feature best practices&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage and develop a team of talented Product Managers&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What We’re Looking For&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Previous work experience with free-to-play games&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong leadership skills.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong quantitative and qualitative analytical ability with attention to detail.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Understanding of game design concepts and principles.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience hitting revenue/metric targets on a live game.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to thrive in a fast-paced environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Passion for figuring out how game economies work.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong verbal and written communication skills.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;An MBA or a Degree in Economics, Business, Statistics, Data Analytics, or Finance is a plus.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Scopely, we create games for everyone - and want to ensure that the people behind our games reflect that! We are committed to creating a diverse, supportive work environment where everyone is treated with respect. We are committed to providing equal employment opportunities and welcome individuals from all backgrounds to join us &amp;amp; embrace the adventure!&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Please ensure that the résumé/CV you attach is written in English.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;About Scopely&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Scopely is a leading video game and global interactive entertainment company, home to many of the world’s most beloved and enduring experiences, including two of the most successful mobile games of all-time “MONOPOLY GO!” and “Pokémon GO,” along with “Stumble Guys,” “Star Trek™ Fleet Command,” “MARVEL Strike Force,” “WWE Champions,” the Scrabble® franchise, “Yahtzee® With Buddies,” and many others. Across mobile, web, PC, and console, Scopely creates, develops, publishes, and live-operates one of the most diversified and award-winning portfolios in the games industry — bringing hundreds of millions of players together through a shared love of play.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Founded in 2011, Scopely is powered by its exceptional team — including thousands of world-class gamemakers around the globe, a distinctive tenet-driven culture, and its proprietary technology platform, Playgami. Together, these strengths have fueled Scopely’s position as the #1 mobile games company in the U.S. and #2 globally, generating more than $10 billion in lifetime revenue. Whether building global sensations like “MONOPOLY GO!” from the ground up, or expanding through strategic acquisitions, including the FoxNext, GSN, and Scopely Explore games businesses — Scopely consistently delivers experiences players love today and return to for years to come.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Recognized multiple times as one of the &quot;100 Most Influential Companies in the World&quot; by TIME magazine and one of Fast Company&#39;s &quot;World&#39;s Most Innovative Companies&quot; and “Best Workplaces for Innovators,” Scopely believes that video games can be a force for good — creating meaningful connections, vibrant communities, and making life better through play.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Scopely has global operations and partners across four continents in more than a dozen countries worldwide. For more information, visit: &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.scopely.com/&quot;&gt;https://www.scopely.com/&lt;/a&gt;.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Notice to Candidates: Scopely will never request payment or financial information during the application or hiring process. Please apply only through our official &lt;a href=&quot;http://scopely.com&quot;&gt;website&lt;/a&gt; and verify that all Talent Partner communications come from an email address ending in @&lt;a href=&quot;http://scopely.com&quot;&gt;scopely.com&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Should you have any questions or encounter any fraudulent requests/emails/websites, please immediately contact ----- Our job applicant privacy policies are available here: &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.scopely.com/en/job-applicant-privacy-notice-for-ca-residents&quot;&gt;California Privacy Notice&lt;/a&gt; and &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.scopely.com/en/eea-and-uk-job-applicant-privacy-notice&quot;&gt;EEA/UK Privacy Notice&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Employment at Scopely is based solely on a person&#39;s merit and qualifications. Scopely does not discriminate against any employee or applicant because of race, creed, color, religion, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition (including breastfeeding), or any other basis protected by law. We also consider qualified applicants with arrest or conviction records, consistent with applicable federal, state and local law.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;<p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>

&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Some key info for you about Liberis:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;🌱 We were founded in 2007&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;💰 We have provided over $3bn of funding to small businesses so far&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;🚀 We have been named in&lt;span class=&quot;Apple-converted-space&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;strong&gt;CNBC &amp;amp; Statista Top 150 UK Fintechs for 2025&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;🌍 We&#39;re a global team, with a dynamic presence in&lt;span class=&quot;Apple-converted-space&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;strong&gt;6&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;Apple-converted-space&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;key locations around the world&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;🧠 We&#39;re a thriving community of over&lt;span class=&quot;Apple-converted-space&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;strong&gt;290&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;Apple-converted-space&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;innovative minds&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;👩🏾 🤝 👨🏼 We&#39;re a vibrant melting pot, celebrating over&lt;span class=&quot;Apple-converted-space&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;strong&gt;27&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;Apple-converted-space&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;nationalities in our team&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;🏢 Our team brings experience from over&lt;span class=&quot;Apple-converted-space&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;strong&gt;740&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;Apple-converted-space&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;previous companies, from startups to global giants&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;🎯 We have just been named as one of&lt;span class=&quot;Apple-converted-space&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;strong&gt;FinTech’s Finest 50&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;Apple-converted-space&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;by Welcome to the Jungle&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;💪 We’re proud to be an accredited&lt;span class=&quot;Apple-converted-space&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Real Living Wage&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;Apple-converted-space&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;employer, ensuring everyone is paid fairly for the great work they do!&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Our Product &amp;amp; Engineering Team:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Liberis is building the embedded finance platform that lets partners around the world offer innovative funding products to their small business customers. We&#39;re a growth-stage fintech with teams in London, Nottingham, Atlanta, Stockholm, Munich and Mumbai, and we’re building a global Product, Data &amp;amp; Engineering team that thrives on autonomy, ownership, and is focused on impact! Our teams solve real-world problems for small businesses, shaping products that unlock opportunity at scale.&lt;span class=&quot;Apple-converted-space&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Engineering is going through an AI-first transformation, rethinking how teams are structured and how they ship. It&#39;s changing what a small team can do! We empower our teams to make decisions, move fast, and take full responsibility for the solutions they deliver. You’ll join a team where curiosity is encouraged and collaboration across Product, Data, Delivery and Engineering is the norm.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;The team&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You’ll join Liberis’ Product Design team, working alongside product managers, engineers, and researchers across the business to help shape exceptional financial experiences to support small business!&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;The role&amp;nbsp;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re looking for a Product Designer to help evolve the internal systems our teams rely on and the service journeys that connect them to our merchants and partners. You’ll take ownership of design problems from discovery through to shipped, polished interfaces, partnering closely with product managers and engineers along the way!&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a hands-on role focused primarily on design delivery within our fulfilment area. You’ll work on complex workflows and internal systems used by teams including Operations, Underwriting and Collections, turning an established product vision into well-considered features that can be shipped in manageable increments. Success in this role looks like well-crafted, research informed interfaces that ship on time!&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You’ll join a collaborative environment with engaged users and a strong front-end engineering team. Because the people using your work are close to the product team, you’ll have regular opportunities to understand their needs, test ideas and see the immediate impact of what you deliver.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;What you’ll get to do in the role:&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Liberis, our internal systems are at the core of how we support small businesses. In this role, you&#39;ll design and ship the interfaces our operational teams rely on every day, turning complex workflows into clear, usable tools.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You&#39;ll partner closely with your Product Manager and Engineering Manager throughout the product lifecycle, from discovery and early concepts through to delivery and post-launch iteration, shaping decisions together rather than handing off a finished design.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You&#39;ll build and iterate on high-fidelity UI in Figma, taking designs from early wireframes through to pixel-perfect, developer-ready screens, and take ownership of our design system, keeping components and patterns consistent across the product.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You&#39;ll work directly with the operational teams who use these systems day to day, running interviews and usability testing to understand where the friction is, and mapping their end-to-end journeys to find where processes break down and spot opportunities to fix them.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;What we think you’ll need:&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You’re comfortable facilitating UX research and communicating findings clearly to validate your decisions for new product features.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You think strategically about the long-term implications of design decisions and are used to planning well beyond the feature immediately required to ensure products continue to evolve with clear direction.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong Figma experience is essential for this role, including knowledge of component best practice, auto layout and variant management. Experience using developer handover features would also be highly beneficial.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Your design process is highly collaborative; you iterate openly and validate quickly with feedback from stakeholders and design peers before aligning on a path forward.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You are comfortable working alongside engineers to turn designs into shipped product features, with an awareness of feasibility and technical dependencies. You judge your work by what’s shipped, not what’s in your design file.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to prototype at pace with a high level of interactivity and attention to detail to bring designs to life for stakeholders and users.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience running usability testing and validating that products meet user expectations and adhere to WCAG accessibility standards.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Knowledge of service design strategies including service blueprints, user journey maps and identifying opportunities across multi-channel processes.
&lt;div class=&quot;p-rich_text_section&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Next steps&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;Apple-converted-space&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;If this opportunity feels like the right fit for your next career move, we’d love to hear from you!&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Even if you don’t meet every requirement, don’t hesitate to apply or reach out to Chess (Internal Recruiter) on&lt;span class=&quot;Apple-converted-space&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;a ----------
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;p-rich_text_section&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong data-stringify-type=&quot;bold&quot;&gt;Our hybrid approach&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Working together in person helps us move faster, collaborate better, and build a great Liberis culture. Our hybrid working policy requires team members to be in the office at least 3 days a week. At Liberis, we embrace flexibility as a core part of our culture, while also valuing the importance of the time our teams spend together in the office.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;#LI-FC1&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
