&lt;p&gt;Captify, now part of Verve Group, is the leading Search Intelligence Platform for the open web and the largest independent holder of first-party search data outside of Google, connecting the real-time searches from over 2 billion devices globally. Its Search Intelligence technology powers omnichannel programmatic advertising and real-time insights for the world’s biggest brands, such as Disney, Unilever, eBay, Mercedes-Benz, Microsoft, Nestlé, GSK, Uber, Mars, P&amp;amp;G, Sony and Toyota—without reliance on third-party cookies. Captify brings brands more customers, publishers greater yield and consumers the most relevant digital experiences.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What we&#39;re looking for&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are seeking a dynamic and client-focused Account Manager to join our team.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Account Manager will act as the primary point of contact between clients/agencies and internal teams, ensuring seamless coordination and successful delivery of campaigns aligned with client objectives and KPIs.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This role requires strong client relationship management, excellent organisational skills, and commercial awareness. You will be responsible for managing multiple projects across omnichannel digital campaigns, including OLV, Display, and CTV, ensuring high-quality execution and consistent communication across all stakeholders.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;em&gt;This is a hybrid position with three days per week in our London Office (Covent Garden).&amp;nbsp;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll be doing:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Client Relationship Management&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and maintain strong day-to-day relationships with clients with a key focus on retention&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Understand client campaign objectives, campaign goals and brand positioning&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Act as the primary point of contact for all campaign related communications such as campaign set ups, troubleshooting and identifying oppurtunities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support senior team members in delivering quarterly business reviews (QBRs) and strategic account reviews&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage client expectations and ensure high levels of satisfaction&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Campaign &amp;amp; Account Management&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the end-to-end campaign lifecycle, including internal briefing, checking accurate trafficking and QA, support for trader optimisation, in-flight reporting, and post-campaign analysis.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Coordinate campaign delivery across internal teams ensuring timelines, budgets, and objectives are met&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Monitor campaign performance and provide actionable insights through weekly reporting and PCAs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain accurate account documentation including briefs, status trackers, and campaign summaries&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Consitently identify opportunities for account growth and upselling services&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Internal Collaboration&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Act as the central point of contact between external clients and internal departments (Trading, Ad Ops, Creative, Insights, etc.)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Help to idenity internal platform gaps, challeneges or client needs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure internal teams are aligned with client expectations and deliverables&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience using programmatic platforms (DSPs/SSPs) for campaign delivery and reporting&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience using CRM and reporting tools such as Salesforce&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience using data visualisation platforms like Tableau (or similar)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to interpret campaign performance data and translate it into clear, insight-led recommendations and client-ready presentations (PCA decks)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you need to be successful:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;1-2+ years of experience in account management and/or client services, preferably within a media, advertising, or agency environment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A good understanding of the digital advertising ecosystem, including media types and buys&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience supporting or managing omnichannel campaigns across digital channels (e.g. display, online video, and rich media formats)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent communication, presentation, and stakeholder management skills, with confidence in client-facing situations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong organisational skills with the ability to manage multiple clients, deadlines, and internal stakeholders simultaneously&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfortable working in fast-paced, deadline-driven environments with competing priorities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proficiency in Microsoft Office and Google Workspace (especially Excel/Sheets and PowerPoint/Slides for reporting and presentations)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What We Offer&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Just a few of the benefits waiting for you at Verve:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Stay healthy with our&lt;strong&gt; Bupa HealthCare Plan&lt;/strong&gt; with easy access to medical care&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support your long-term financial security with our &lt;strong&gt;Aviva Corporate Pension Scheme&lt;/strong&gt;, with Verve contributing 5% of your qualifying earnings&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Pick what matters most to you in our &lt;strong&gt;Personalized Benefits Platform, &lt;/strong&gt;with a budget of&lt;strong&gt;&amp;nbsp; &lt;/strong&gt;£50/month&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Recharge with &lt;strong&gt;25 paid vacation days + 3 Wellness days &lt;/strong&gt;throughout the year, in addition to the public holidays&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Boost your professional knowledge with our annual training budget &amp;amp; internal webinars&lt;/strong&gt;… and even more reasons to join us!&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 8pt;&quot;&gt;Verve provides equal employment opportunities to all employees and applicants for employment and prohibits discrimination and harassment of any type without regard to race, color, religion, age, sex, national origin, disability status, genetics, protected veteran status, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, or any other characteristic protected by federal, state or local laws.&amp;nbsp;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;If you are a California resident subject to the California Consumer Privacy Act, &lt;a href=&quot;https://verve.com/california-applicant-privacy-notice/&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;click here&lt;/a&gt; to understand how Verve processes your personal information and how you can exercise your rights.&lt;br&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 8pt;&quot;&gt;If you are located in the EU or UK visit our&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;a style=&quot;font-size: 8pt;&quot; href=&quot;https://verve.com/applicant-privacy-policy/&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;privacy policy&lt;/a&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 8pt;&quot;&gt; to understand how Verve processes your personal information and how you can exercise your rights.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;<p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>

&lt;p&gt;Captify’s unique search intelligence platform provides brands with a deep understanding of consumer interests, motivations, and intentions in real time, allowing for precise targeting and better campaign measurement. The underlying machine learning technology transforms real search intent into actionable marketing strategies that are used by over 800 leading global brands for programmatic activation, pre-campaign strategies, and unique measurement solutions. Captify is regularly recognised for innovation and excellence in advertising technology.&amp;nbsp; Captify UK recently won Campaign’s Ad Tech provider of the year award.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Captify is part of the Verve Group. Verve for Advertisers is a global, end-to-end advertising technology platform that helps brands and agencies reach target audiences across the open web. Operating as a full-stack ad exchange, it connects buyers with premium publishers across mobile apps, CTV, and digital screens.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What We&#39;re Looking For:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;isSelectedEnd&quot;&gt;This is a strategic commercial role responsible for driving long-term, sustainable revenue growth through the development, expansion and commercialisation of Captify&#39;s data partnerships.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;isSelectedEnd&quot;&gt;The role focuses on identifying and building high-value partnerships that extend the reach of Captify&#39;s data beyond its core media proposition, unlocking new revenue streams, accelerating adoption across strategy, activation and measurement, and enabling the commercial team to bring innovative products and solutions to market.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;isSelectedEnd&quot;&gt;Working cross-functionally with Commercial, Product, Marketing and Legal, this role will shape partnership strategy, negotiate commercial agreements, and build scalable relationships that deliver mutual value and support Captify&#39;s wider business objectives.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The ideal candidate combines deep knowledge of the data and adtech ecosystem with strong commercial acumen, relationship-building skills and a track record of creating strategic partnerships that drive measurable business growth.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You&#39;ll Do:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop and execute Captify&#39;s commercial partnerships strategy, identifying opportunities to drive incremental revenue and expand the reach of Captify&#39;s data solutions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify, qualify and secure new strategic partners across the media, adtech and data ecosystem, with a clear focus on long-term commercial value.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead the end-to-end partnership lifecycle, from opportunity identification and outreach through commercial negotiation, contracting and launch.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build trusted senior-level relationships with partners, gaining a deep understanding of their commercial objectives, data strategies and growth opportunities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop joint business plans that drive adoption, revenue growth and long-term partnership success.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Grow existing partnerships by identifying opportunities to cross-sell, upsell and introduce new products, markets and use cases.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate closely with Captify&#39;s Commercial teams to create shared pipeline opportunities and maximise revenue across all channels where Captify&#39;s data is available.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with Product, Marketing, Legal and other internal stakeholders to ensure partnerships are successfully onboarded, operationalised and supported.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work alongside the Commercial Partnerships Account Manager to ensure partner SLAs are consistently achieved, whilst proactively identifying new opportunities to increase engagement and value.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Monitor market trends, competitor activity and emerging technologies to identify new partnership opportunities and inform commercial strategy.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Act as the internal voice of the partner, sharing market feedback and collaborating with Product teams to influence future product development and innovation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain accurate forecasting, pipeline management and regular reporting on partnership performance, commercial progress and future opportunities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work closely with UK Commercial Leadership to identify partnership opportunities that strengthen and support Captify&#39;s core business and go-to-market strategy.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You&#39;ll Need:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5+ years&#39; experience in commercial partnerships, business development or data sales within media, adtech, martech or digital advertising.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven experience developing and growing strategic commercial partnerships that deliver measurable revenue growth.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong understanding of the digital advertising, audience data and identity landscape.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated success negotiating complex commercial agreements with senior stakeholders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent relationship management skills, with the ability to influence both internal and external stakeholders at all levels.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Commercially minded with strong strategic thinking and problem-solving capabilities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Highly collaborative, with experience working cross-functionally across Commercial, Product, Marketing, Legal and Finance.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent communication, presentation and negotiation skills.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfortable operating in a fast-paced, evolving environment with strong attention to detail.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Willingness to travel for partner meetings, including occasional international travel, while working effectively within a hybrid or remote team.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;div&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What We Offer&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Just a few of the benefits waiting for you at Verve:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Stay healthy with our&lt;strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;Bupa HealthCare Plan&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;with easy access to medical care&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support your long-term financial security with our&amp;nbsp;&lt;strong&gt;Aviva Corporate Pension Scheme&lt;/strong&gt;, with Verve contributing 5% of your qualifying earnings&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Pick what matters most to you in our&amp;nbsp;&lt;strong&gt;Personalized Benefits Platform,&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;with a budget of&lt;strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;£50/month&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Recharge with&amp;nbsp;&lt;strong&gt;25 paid vacation days + 3 Wellness days&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;throughout the year, in addition to the public holidays&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Boost your professional knowledge with our annual training budget &amp;amp; internal webinars&lt;/strong&gt;… and even more reasons to join us!&lt;/p&gt;
